    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱεροσῡλ-έω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱεροσύληκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					417.8
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>):—<i>rob a temple,
				commit sacrilege</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				845
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				575b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. τὰ ὅπλα</span>
			<i>steal the sacred</i> arms, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				57.64
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				136
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. τὰ ἱερά</span>
			<i>rob</i> or <i>plunder</i> the temples, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.26.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phalar.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					84.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
